  "question": {
    "html": "<p>A quantity of an ideal gas is at a temperature T in a cylinder with a movable piston that traps a length L of the gas. The piston is moved so that the length of the trapped gas is reduced to <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\frac{5L}{6}\"></span> and the pressure of the gas doubles.</p>\n<p><figure data-asset-id=\"fig_01\"><img alt=\"Source question diagram 1\" src=\"asset:fig_01\"/></figure></p>\n<p>What is the temperature of the gas at the end of the change?</p>\n<p>[1]</p>\n<ol class=\"mcq-options\"><li data-label=\"A\"><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\frac{5}{12}T\"></span></li><li data-label=\"B\"><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\frac{3}{5}T\"></span></li><li data-label=\"C\"><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\frac{5}{3}T\"></span></li><li data-label=\"D\"><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\frac{12}{5}T\"></span></li></ol>"
  },
